not by the writers. The writers now retry a contended replace (`rebar._store.fsutil.replace_with_retry`, sporting-feudalist-bluet). On Windows, opening a file while `MoveFileEx(MOVEFILE_REPLACE_EXISTING)` replaces it can fail with access denied; POSIX readers never see this.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n- Product readers that open a published sidecar, cache or cursor without holding the writer's lock (for example a store's initial load) can get the same transient `PermissionError` on Windows and treat it as a failed or empty read.\n- Readers that already read under the sibling lock (`sidecar_transactions.mutate_json_object`) are unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The product read paths of files published through `atomic_write`/`replace_with_retry` are enumerated, and each is recorded as either lock-protected or exposed on Windows.\n- [ ] Every exposed read path tolerates the transient refusal (or is shown not to need to), with a Windows-branch unit test.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"2781-42c5-201c-4efe","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows: readers of an atomically replaced file can get PermissionError while a replace is in flight","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e7ea735b-87d1-4bd8-b3f4-6c87435c7281","fddbe6bf-38ad-4a34-b884-5aee4e75e907"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795066663296898450,"uuid":"41e0c106-28b7-4042-8fd0-84a3da4061c5"}